      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.noOp",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        480,
        120
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Assumptions\n\n- Generic **Webhook** POST `telegram`; payload uses `message.text` at the root or under `body` (Telegram update shape).\n- **Start Command** IF: `/start` gets a fixed greeting via **Send Telegram Reply** without OpenAI; other text goes to OpenAI.\n- JAW-9925: keyword rules are documented on **Send to OpenAI** via per-node `notes` + `notesInFlow` (not an extra sticky); content reflects text/non-text and `/start` only—no product keyword list or message-id dedup in this file.\n- Inbound auth: **httpHeaderAuth** credential named **Telegram API** (maps to Telegram `secret_token` header); outbound send uses **telegramApi** with the same display name.\n- OpenAI: **gpt-4o-mini**, user message only, maxTokens 500; **3 retries**, **5s** between tries.\n- **chatId**: from `message.chat.id` (or documented fallbacks); Telegram updates must include `chat`—no fixed env fallback for outbound send.\n- Errors (JAW-9926): **Send to OpenAI** / **Send Telegram Reply** error outputs → **Prepare Error Log** (`stage`, `errorMessage` ≤200 chars, `at` ISO) → **Notify Administrator** to **$env.TELEGRAM_ADMIN_CHAT_ID** (3 retries, 5s); no user message text or chat ids in the alert. Failed notify ends at **Notification Delivery Failed**.\n- Non-text updates end at **Ignore Non-Text** without error."
      },
      "id": "f2a3b4c5-6d7e-8f9a-3b4c-5d6e7f8091a2",
      "name": "Assumptions",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -40,
        -240
      ]
    }
  ],
